## 1. Executive Summary

A phishing email disguised as an urgent Exchange Server 2019 security advisory delivers a PowerShell payload that, once run by the victim, executes a full intrusion chain: defense tampering, extensive host and domain reconnaissance, dual persistence, credential access, command-and-control beaconing, log clearing, and impact — consistent with a ransomware-precursor operation.

## 2. Delivery

| ID | Technique | Observed |
|---|---|---|
| T1566.001 | Phishing: Spearphishing Attachment | Email themed as an Exchange 2019 patch advisory |
| T1204.002 | User Execution: Malicious File | Victim runs the attached/linked script |

## 3. Execution & Defense Evasion

| ID | Technique | Observed |
|---|---|---|
| T1059.001 | PowerShell | Entire payload is a PowerShell script |
| T1070.001 | Indicator Removal: Clear Windows Event Logs | Security, System and Application logs cleared |

## 4. Discovery

Broad enumeration precedes action: local accounts and group membership, domain and forest identity, network configuration and active connections, running services, local security policy, and Group Policy results. Maps to T1087 (Account Discovery), T1069 (Permission Groups Discovery), T1016 (System Network Configuration Discovery), T1049 (System Network Connections Discovery), T1007 (System Service Discovery), T1615 (Group Policy Discovery).

